@*
    The document the package's own search page is rendered in when the site has no layout it can be
    rendered into. Deliberately bare: the page itself carries all of its styling, and a site that
    wants its own header and footer around search does not use this at all - it names one of its own
    pages in Search → Settings, or renders the search page's view component from its own template.

    This exists as a layout rather than as markup in the page because <head> and <body> have to be
    real elements for a tag helper component to find them: that is how the search box's stylesheet
    and the type-ahead script arrive on this page, the same way they arrive on every page of a site.
*@
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>@(ViewData["Title"] as string ?? "Search")</title>
</head>
<body>
    @RenderBody()
</body>
</html>
